{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Fallen, with eyes unveiled.</b> Its plain sense is as the Targum renders — that it appeared to him only at night, when he was lying down. Its midrash: when it was revealed to him he had no strength to stand on his feet, and fell on his face, because he was uncircumcised, and it was abhorrent to be revealed to him upright, standing before Him."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:31.079885452Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}